onciliation, stale plans, record collisions, and conflicting second admission fail closed."},"id":"pems:proposition:51e90663956c93402e7424f1","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a9de97648bc02bbae28708b2"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The cross-adapter tests verify Human-Agent and CLI surfaces preserve identical proposal, approval, D3, workflow, grant, event, continuation, and delegable-apply artifacts/results when routing the same operations."},"id":"pems:proposition:52b92ba6950ffc588ceb7c71","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a43e753abaf669e2a70ea588"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The exceptional-recovery tests verify valid history cannot be recovered, recovery is protected-root and evidence-backed, changed damage after approval fails closed, and later damage mutation is detected by recovery records."},"id":"pems:proposition:5473a0e16aaa087e37908ddd","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:9096573a3347bbc16d191db4"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The automation-boundary tests verify materiality cannot be bypassed by an in-scope grant and is revalidated before grant consumption."},"id":"pems:proposition:5a7d03e54c5e66e3b7c1a8f3","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:9d6aee67f4434e191c8e91e6"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The automation-boundary tests verify stale state, exhausted or revoked grants, unresolved activation/conditions, grant ambiguity, wildcard inference, scope expansion, and protected operations all stop automation fail closed."},"id":"pems:proposition:5e5731deeade4b9631566281","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:9d6aee67f4434e191c8e91e6"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The reconciliation tests verify activation authority is required, candidates must come from submissions, successful reconciliation persists immutable disposition and activation evidence, and no admission/canonical state is created."},"id":"pems:proposition:6cbbf81941480a7592aac79c","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:618918c80883dc5426c6869f"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The status tests verify lifecycle blockers have precedence, missing projections are classified rebuildable without mutation, authorization scopes remain independent, evidence/candidate presence never asserts semantic validity, and status is strictly read-only."},"id":"pems:proposition:6f2f04b267f12d5208a538e4","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:1d559d638588232963b8c4d9"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The admission tests verify that admission requires independent admission authority and that a reconciliation recommendation alone is not admission authority."},"id":"pems:proposition:8ca3212ec1e07a740e882d5d","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a9de97648bc02bbae28708b2"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The role-registry tests verify default Steward role presence does not create authority, role planning is deterministic, scoped snapshots affect only roles within scope, and forbidden protocol/package roles or unknown rd capabilities are rejected."},"id":"pems:proposition:961c609362ac7e2594794083","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:7140dbd7083e02e1bd7040ad"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The authority-grant tests verify grant definitions are immutable, content-addressed, and idempotent and that non-delegable operations fail closed at grant creation."},"id":"pems:proposition:99347c752acedad22dc43250","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:e3ec9042829ec1165fd44b32"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The shared-orchestration tests verify delegable operator and role proposals can auto-advance through a common path while stale D3, materiality pauses, ambiguous grants, and workflow scope failures stop before grant consumption."},"id":"pems:proposition:a7f7301047ce92780c3b3dba","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:6ca2c409b0deb4f35174ef88"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The Steward-authorization tests verify scopes begin unassigned, the default Steward is not automatic, authorization scopes are independent, and reassignment/revocation affect only the selected scope."},"id":"pems:proposition:aac8873d8b2a3ffddaecd389","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:8811bfdfc6800a669619d933"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The workflow tests verify immutable definition identity binds intent/authentication, auto-advance requires explicit prospective confirmation, extension events do not advance the normative head, and competing normative transitions fail stale-head checks."},"id":"pems:proposition:b0712f9cdb6e277d6eb6896f","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:9b0561842b7595251d9f4608"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The authority-grant tests verify approval limits are consumed at issuance, revocation blocks future issuance without invalidating past approval, and issuance/revocation use exact-head concurrency."},"id":"pems:proposition:b514f9c1f202fc360fc23aaa","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:e3ec9042829ec1165fd44b32"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The authority-grant tests verify an exact proposal must be wholly contained by grant scope and that partial/unknown effects, workflow mismatch, terminal workflow state, stale D3, and materiality pauses block issuance."},"id":"pems:proposition:c4897fd559415c3ebe8e3fb0","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:e3ec9042829ec1165fd44b32"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The workflow tests verify materiality pauses suspend continuation, acknowledgements bind exact pauses, completion is primitive-proved and terminal, cancellation is requester/root-only, and revisions create successors while sealing predecessors."},"id":"pems:proposition:c914cb031c234d3ee364b9e7","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:9b0561842b7595251d9f4608"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The initial-operator tests verify an empty project requires an initial operator ceremony, planning is deterministic and mutation-free, exact confirmation is required, and application creates exactly one protected root."},"id":"pems:proposition:d3bb88c695ddded38acc57cf","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a4711dbb6eb553b24136f07b"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The activation tests verify fail-closed behavior for malformed evidence, unknown activation methods, unassigned scopes, unavailable authorized roles, and conflicting authorization projections."},"id":"pems:proposition:d502a6cc88fced73af226f73","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:b761b8e2941993b69b73e300"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The autonomous-workflow tests verify a prospectively authorized chain can complete without Human interruption only while its accepted scope remains valid, with materiality, scope expansion, and protected authority causing interruption before the next consequential mutation."},"id":"pems:proposition:d59fb5ac65b5671a7cfaaf51","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:9e73ca1bf0d5a449abb264bb"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The admission tests verify first admission requires explicit project identity and successful first admission writes schema-valid project-seeded PEMS/COVE plus immutable evidence."},"id":"pems:proposition:d8371ae110a7202452968848","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:a9de97648bc02bbae28708b2"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The role-registry tests verify unauthorized operators and conflicting projections fail closed and role changes create no semantic authority or canonical state."},"id":"pems:proposition:d928a97b8d16e58762e2786c","kind":"proposition","lifecycle":"current","provenance":{"primary":["pems:source_observation:7140dbd7083e02e1bd7040ad"]}},{"data":{"epistemic_role":"asserted","proposition_kind":"observation","statement":"The mutation tests verify consumed approvals cannot authorize later transitions, stale bases fail without mutation, missing projections are rebuildable, conflicting projections fail closed, and corrupted/non-contiguous event chains are detected."},"id":"pems:proposition:df65510d9622fe0d5d05ba7e","kind":"p